ion; the blueprint has no `\\lean` link, so the node remains informal by design.\n### hgraph/nodes/48388eca7f61/comment-3.md\n---\nauthor: horizon\ncreated: '2026-08-27T19:46:54'\ndate: '2026-08-27T19:46:54'\nprovenance:\n  projects: Mumford\n  role: horizon\n  round: '2'\n  rounds: '3'\n  run: '0165'\n  session: 0006-horizon-fs-mumford\n  task: fs-mumford\n  task_title: Advance Mumford Abelian Varieties formalization\nupdated: '2026-08-27T19:46:54'\n---\nUniformization/lean adds a genus-indexed real torus model with 2g factors. Under an explicit additive uniformization witness, its nonzero-integer torsion is additively equivalent to (Fin (2g) → ZMod |n|), has cardinality |n|^(2g), and is divisible; the analytic existence of such a witness remains separate.### hgraph/nodes/48388eca7f61/comment-4.md\n---\nauthor: horizon\ncreated: '2026-08-27T20:21:54'\ndate: '2026-08-27T20:21:54'\nprovenance:\n  projects: Mumford\n  role: horizon\n  round: '2'\n  rounds: '3'\n  run: '0165'\n  session: 0006-horizon-fs-mumford\n  task: fs-mumford\n  task_title: Advance Mumford Abelian Varieties formalization\ntitle: Finite torsion packaging\nupdated: '2026-08-27T20:21:54'\n---\nUniformization.lean now also proves that the nonzero-integer torsion subgroup is finite by transporting the existing AddEquiv to the finite product of ZMod factors (commit 66f33874a5). The chosen uniformization witness remains explicit.### hgraph/nodes/48388eca7f61/comment-5.md\n---\nauthor: horizon\ncreated: '2026-08-27T23:00:47'\ndate: '2026-08-27T23:00:47'\nprovenance:\n  projects: Mumford\n  role: horizon\n  round: '0'\n  rounds: '24'\n  run: 0180\n  session: 0002-horizon-fs-mumford\n  task: fs-mumford\n  task_title: Advance Mumford Abelian Varieties formalization\ntitle: Verified torsion interface (run 0180)\nupdated: '2026-08-27T23:00:47'\n---\nUniformization.lean now supplies the explicit DivisibleBy witness, scalar-divisibility inclusions, functorial torsion maps, finite cardinality transport, and the natural-cardinality corollary; Analytic.lean supplies the coordinatewise integer-torsion characterization. The analytic uniformization witness remains an explicit assumption, and the frozen blueprint has no \\lean link, so this source node intentionally remains lean_status=empty while the generated Lean declarations are tracked separately."}, {"type": "input_text", "text": "---\n---\nauthor: sync\nchapter: Analytic Theory\ncontent_type: theorem\ncreated: '2026-08-27T16:28:25'\ngenerated: blueprint\nlabel: mumford-frag-uniformization\nlean_status: empty\norder: 1\nref: M:ch1:I.1\ntitle: Uniformization\ntype: tex\nupdated: '2026-08-27T16:28:25'\n---\nThe exponential map $\\exp:V\\to X$ is a surjective homomorphism of complex\nLie groups with kernel a lattice $U$ in $V$, and induces an isomorphism\n$V/U\\simeq X$.---\nauthor: sync\nchapter: Analytic Theory\ncontent_type: theorem\ncreated: '2026-08-27T16:28:25'\ngenerated: blueprint\nlabel: mumford-frag-commutative\nlean_status: empty\norder: 0\nref: M:ch1:I.1\ntitle: Commutativity of a compact connected complex Lie group\ntype: tex\nupdated: '2026-08-27T16:28:25'\n---\nLet $X$ be a compact connected complex Lie group.  Then $X$ is commutative.---\nauthor: sync\nchapter: Analytic Theory\ncontent_type: theorem\ncreated: '2026-08-27T16:28:25'\ngenerated: blueprint\nlabel: mumford-frag-integral-cohomology\nlean_status: empty\norder: 3\nref: M:ch1:I.1\ntitle: Integral cohomology\ntype: tex\nupdated: '2026-08-27T16:28:25'\n---\nThere are canonical isomorphisms\n\\[\n H^r(X,\\mathbf Z)\\simeq\n \\{\\text{alternating $r$-forms }U\\times\\cdots\\times U\\to\\mathbf Z\\}.\n\\]---\nauthor: sync\nchapter: Algebraic Theory via Varieties\ncontent_type: corollary\ncreated: '2026-08-27T16:28:25'\ngenerated: blueprint\nlabel: mumford-cor-divisible-finite-torsion\nlean_status: empty\norder: 65\nref: M:ch2:II.7\ntitle: Divisibility and finite torsion\ntype: tex\nupdated: '2026-08-27T16:28:25'\n---\nAn abelian variety $X$ is divisible and 