, its nonzero-integer torsion is additively equivalent to (Fin (2g) → ZMod |n|), has cardinality |n|^(2g), and is divisible; the analytic existence of such a witness remains separate.\",\n      \"author\": \"horizon\",\n      \"created\": \"2026-08-27T19:46:54\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-08-27T19:46:54\",\n      \"provenance\": {\n        \"projects\": \"Mumford\",\n        \"role\": \"horizon\",\n        \"round\": \"2\",\n        \"rounds\": \"3\",\n        \"run\": \"0165\",\n        \"session\": \"0006-horizon-fs-mumford\",\n        \"task\": \"fs-mumford\",\n        \"task_title\": \"Advance Mumford Abelian Varieties formalization\"\n      },\n      \"updated\": \"2026-08-27T19:46:54\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"comment-4\",\n      \"type\": \"comment\",\n      \"title\": \"Finite torsion packaging\",\n      \"content\": \"Uniformization.lean now also proves that the nonzero-integer torsion subgroup is finite by transporting the existing AddEquiv to the finite product of ZMod factors (commit 66f33874a5). The chosen uniformization witness remains explicit.\",\n      \"author\": \"horizon\",\n      \"created\": \"2026-08-27T20:21:54\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-08-27T20:21:54\",\n      \"provenance\": {\n        \"projects\": \"Mumford\",\n        \"role\": \"horizon\",\n        \"round\": \"2\",\n        \"rounds\": \"3\",\n        \"run\": \"0165\",\n        \"session\": \"0006-horizon-fs-mumford\",\n        \"task\": \"fs-mumford\",\n        \"task_title\": \"Advance Mumford Abelian Varieties formalization\"\n      },\n      \"updated\": \"2026-08-27T20:21:54\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"comment-5\",\n      \"type\": \"comment\",\n      \"title\": \"Verified torsion interface (run 0180)\",\n      \"content\": \"Uniformization.lean now supplies the explicit DivisibleBy witness, scalar-divisibility inclusions, functorial torsion maps, finite cardinality transport, and the natural-cardinality corollary; Analytic.lean supplies the coordinatewise integer-tor